<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catiline</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 108–62 BCE</span> · Also known as Lucius Sergius Catilina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Catiline (Lucius Sergius Catilina) was a Roman patrician politician who, after failing to win the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">consulship</a>, organised a conspiracy to seize power in 63 BCE. The consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a> exposed the plot in his speeches against Catiline, using evidence obtained with the help of envoys of the Allobroges, and several conspirators in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> were executed. Catiline fell in battle at Pistoria in early 62 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catiline.jpg" alt="Catiline" width="296" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cesare Maccari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicero_Denounces_Catiline_in_the_Roman_Senate_by_Cesare_Maccari_-_detail_of_Catilina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
